# S1c: the packed GDN pieces at the four-card widths on one card (QWEN_FAST_TP=4), watcher pass: the first hardware run of the
# _tp sibling DMA kernels at 192 / 80 pages, K5 at 12 value heads and the 48-core user-batch launch, under the NoC sanitiser so an
# out-of-range DMA is a named error, not a hang that costs a reset.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): 10-20 min (one seed, no iterations; the container timeout is 45 min).
# Read the GDN_TP4 verdict line (reduced scope) and the watcher log: no error or assert lines.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--seeds 17 --prefixes 0,16 --iterations 0
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=gdn_tp4 TP4_WIDTH=4 WATCHER=1 KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7
